invariant: INV-33
file: webpki.c
catches: webpki_auth_test
reason: under pins alone the key read for the pin comes from the chain's
  last entry instead of its leaf, so a pin on an intermediate or root key
  passes the pin check, which RFC 7858 §4.2 and docs/decisions.md 65
  refuse: with no anchor and no name, a CA key pin would accept any
  certificate that CA issued. test/webpki_leaf_pins.h's intermediate-pin
  rows, which want bad_certificate, object.

--- old
        rc = webpki_read_entry(&r, CH_WEBPKI_CERT_MAX, &cert, &cert_len, alert);
        if (rc != CH_OK) {
--- new
        rc = webpki_read_entry(&r, CH_WEBPKI_CERT_MAX, leaf, leaf_len, alert);
        (void)cert;
        (void)cert_len;
        if (rc != CH_OK) {
